gcm/fp: honour the fragment program's per-source input precision modifiers (LD_NO_SRC_PREC=1 old).

From Killzone 2's patch 2094 (Project Pyrrhus, commit 61dcf86, 2026-10-21), ported to KZ3's tree under a free number;
the decoder change is the same, KZ3 adds the one-time "[fp-prec]" log line.

Cause: DWORD2 (SRC1) bits 19-27 hold a 3-bit input precision modifier per source (19-21 SRC0, 22-24 SRC1, 25-27
SRC2; RPCS3's src0/1/2_prec_mod). The hardware clamps the operand to the precision's range after abs and before
negate. The decompiler ignored the field, so a source the program meant as saturated ([0, 1]) or fixed9 ([-1, 1])
reached the arithmetic unclamped. In KZ2 the soft-particle fade (MUL r2.w, r0, |r2| with SRC1 modifier 3) drew every
smoke puff over distant scenery as saturated white.

KZ3 (pass 116 scan of 99 unique fragment programs dumped from K2/K4 draws, scan script of pass 116): 89 carry a
non-zero field; the effective ones (1-4) are on MAD/MUL/ADD/DP3 sources (modifier 4 saturate on 38 instructions,
3 fixed9 on 5); the most common value, 5 on NRM's SRC0 (268 instructions), is left unchanged as RPCS3 does.

Fix: decode the three modifiers on non-branch instructions and wrap the source in clamp() after abs: 1 half
(+-65504), 2 fixed12 [-2, 2], 3 fixed9 [-1, 1], 4 saturate [0, 1]; 0 and other values unchanged. ASSUMPTION: the
ranges of values 1, 2 and 4 follow the destination precision field's meaning. The shader disk cache is keyed by the
HLSL text, so the switch needs no key change. Host test: tools/smoke/test_fp_src_prec.sh.
Behaviour follows RPCS3 (GPL-2.0), src0_prec_mod / src1_prec_mod / src2_prec_mod in its fragment-program decoder;
read, not copied. Upstream candidate (any title).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 154): v0.19 has the per-source precision modifiers itself (Src.prec, fp_src_prec_clamp, FP_SRC*_PREC_SHIFT, the clamp in emit_src, the decode in the instruction loop; same ranges and order: abs, clamp, negate). What stays of this patch is the LD_NO_SRC_PREC=1 switch (fp_src_prec_mode, the '[fp-prec]' line) that tools/smoke/test_fp_src_prec.sh uses; the decode runs only when the switch is not set.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
index 18620af..719ada0 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
@@ -358,6 +358,16 @@ typedef struct {
 #define FP_SRC1_PREC_SHIFT  22
 #define FP_SRC2_PREC_SHIFT  25
 
+/* KZ3 patch 2124: LD_NO_SRC_PREC=1 ignores the modifiers (the output before they were decoded). */
+static int fp_src_prec_mode(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) {
+        const char* e = getenv("LD_NO_SRC_PREC"); on = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 0 : 1;
+        fprintf(stderr, "[fp-prec] source precision modifiers %s\n", on ? "on" : "off (LD_NO_SRC_PREC=1)");
+    }
+    return on;
+}
 static const char* fp_src_prec_clamp(int prec)
 {
     switch (prec) {
@@ -947,7 +957,7 @@ static int rsx_fp_decompile_internal(
         const int src2_abs = fp_src2_abs_mode();
         if ((w3 & FP_SRC2_ABS) && !(w2 & FP_BRANCH)) fp_src2_abs_note(opcode);
         decode_src(w3, src2_abs ? (int)(w3 & FP_SRC2_ABS) : 0, &s2);
-        if (!(w2 & FP_BRANCH)) {   /* a branch's DWORD2 holds other fields */
+        if (!(w2 & FP_BRANCH) && fp_src_prec_mode()) {   /* patch 2124 switch; a branch's DWORD2 holds other fields */
             s0.prec = (int)((w2 >> FP_SRC0_PREC_SHIFT) & 7u);
             s1.prec = (int)((w2 >> FP_SRC1_PREC_SHIFT) & 7u);
             s2.prec = (int)((w2 >> FP_SRC2_PREC_SHIFT) & 7u);
